---
name: waves
description: >-
  Define and use JRebirth Waves for decoupled messaging between components.
  Use for cross-feature notifications, app-wide refresh triggers, or decoupled
  orchestration, not for plain local method calls.
---
# Use Waves

Waves carry typed messages between components that should not know about each other directly. Use them to decouple communication across feature boundaries.

## Good uses

- Cross-feature notifications (e.g., "an item was deleted" broadcast to multiple listeners).
- App-wide refresh triggers when several components need to react to the same event.
- Decoupled orchestration where the sender must not depend on the receiver.

## Bad uses

- Replacing every direct collaboration with message passing. If component A always and only communicates with component B, a direct call or a shared Model property is simpler and clearer.
- Using a Wave for a local call that could be a normal method invocation within the same component.

## Key API

- Declare a `@Preload` interface to hold the wave contract. This makes the wave types discoverable.
- Declare a `String` name constant, then create the wave type: `WaveType NAME_WT = WBuilder.waveType(NAME)`.
- Declare typed payload keys as `WaveItem<T>` constants on the same interface.
- Emit a wave from any component with `sendWave(NAME_WT)` or `sendWave(NAME_WT, WBuilder.waveData(KEY, value))`.
- Receive a wave in any component with `@OnWave(NAME_WT)` on a method.

Template: `templates/WavesTemplate.java.txt`.
